WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
Start with the part you can observe.

00:12.000 --> 00:24.000
Follow the relationship as it changes.

00:24.000 --> 00:36.000
An engine is a chain of jobs: air and fuel release energy, pistons move, and the crankshaft delivers rotation. Cooling and lubrication support that process.

00:36.000 --> 00:48.000
Trace the path: fuel/air → cylinder pressure → piston motion → crankshaft rotation.

00:48.000 --> 01:00.000
Sort components by function

01:00.000 --> 01:12.000
This ideal mechanism leaves out friction, temperature and part-specific behavior. Real designs need measurements.

